Relevant columns / how they might help  

• `comments.text` or `commentsV2.text` : free‑form comment body – a Stack Overflow question URL will appear here.  
• `comments.time_ts` or `commentsV2.timestamp` : filter to comments “on or after 2014‑01‑01”.  
• `comments.id` / `commentsV2.id` : comment id – used only for inspection.  
• `full_partition_extra.url` : the canonical URL stored with a Hacker News item. Some of those items are Stack Overflow questions that were submitted to HN as stories; these rows also contain…  
• `full_partition_extra.tags` : ARRAY<STRING> containing the Stack Overflow tag string (pipe‑delimited).  
• `full_partition_extra.type` : identify rows that are stories ( `type = 'story'` ).  
• `full_partition_extra.timestamp` : used to restrict the window to ≥ 2014 as well.  

Typical conditions we will need  

•  Only comments from 2014‑01‑01 onward    
   `WHERE time_ts >= '2014-01-01'`  

•  Only comments that reference a Stack Overflow question    
   `AND LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'`  

•  Only HN stories that point to Stack Overflow questions and therefore include the tag string  
   `WHERE LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'`  

Below are ten exploratory / progressive SQL snippets (LIMIT 20 each) that one could run in BigQuery to understand the data and arrive at the final result. Replace or remove the final LIMIT in real production queries.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at 20 post‑2013 comments that mention a Stack Overflow question
SELECT id, time_ts, by, text
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
  AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Same inspection but using the newer commentsV2 table
SELECT id, timestamp, by, text
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.commentsV2`
WHERE  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
  AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Extract Stack Overflow question id from comment text
--    (looks for ".../questions/<digits>/")
SELECT
  REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text),
                 r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
  COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
  AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
GROUP BY so_qid
ORDER BY times_mentioned DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same extraction using commentsV2
SELECT
  REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text),
                 r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
  COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.commentsV2`
WHERE  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
  AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
GROUP BY so_qid
ORDER BY times_mentioned DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Combine both comment tables, deduplicate, count mentions
WITH mentions AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
  WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  UNION ALL
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.commentsV2`
  WHERE  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
)
SELECT so_qid, COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
FROM   mentions
GROUP  BY so_qid
ORDER  BY times_mentioned DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Preview HN stories that are actually Stack Overflow questions
SELECT id, url, tags
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.full_partition_extra`
WHERE  type = 'story'
  AND  LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  AND  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Extract Stack Overflow question id and the raw tag string
SELECT
  REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(url), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
  ARRAY_TO_STRING(tags, '|')                AS tag_str
FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.full_partition_extra`
WHERE  type = 'story'
  AND  LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  AND  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Join comment mentions with story rows so we can attach tag_str
WITH mentions AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
         COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
  WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  GROUP  BY so_qid
)
SELECT m.so_qid, m.times_mentioned, s.tag_str
FROM   mentions AS m
JOIN (
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(url), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
         ARRAY_TO_STRING(tags, '|') AS tag_str
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.full_partition_extra`
  WHERE  type = 'story'
    AND  LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
) AS s
USING (so_qid)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Split tag_str, explode into individual tags, weight by times_mentioned
WITH mentions AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
         COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
  WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  GROUP  BY so_qid
),
so_tags AS (
  SELECT
    REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(url), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
    ARRAY_TO_STRING(tags, '|') AS tag_str
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.full_partition_extra`
  WHERE  type = 'story'
    AND  LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
)
SELECT
  tag,
  SUM(times_mentioned) AS total_mentions
FROM   (
  SELECT
    m.times_mentioned,
    SPLIT(t.tag_str, '|') AS tag_arr
  FROM   mentions AS m
  JOIN   so_tags  AS t USING (so_qid)
), UNNEST(tag_arr) AS tag
GROUP BY tag
ORDER BY total_mentions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: top‑10 Stack Overflow tags mentioned in HN comments (≥2014)
WITH comments_unified AS (
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.comments`
  WHERE  time_ts >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
  UNION ALL
  SELECT REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(text), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.commentsV2`
  WHERE  timestamp >= '2014-01-01'
    AND  LOWER(text) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
),
mention_counts AS (
  SELECT so_qid, COUNT(*) AS times_mentioned
  FROM   comments_unified
  GROUP  BY so_qid
),
question_tags AS (
  SELECT
    REGEXP_EXTRACT(LOWER(url), r'/questions/([0-9]+)') AS so_qid,
    ARRAY_TO_STRING(tags, '|') AS tag_str
  FROM   `fh-bigquery.hackernews.full_partition_extra`
  WHERE  type = 'story'
    AND  LOWER(url) LIKE '%stackoverflow.com/questions/%'
)
SELECT
  tag,
  SUM(times_mentioned) AS total_mentions
FROM  (
  SELECT
    mc.times_mentioned,
    SPLIT(qt.tag_str, '|') AS tag_arr
  FROM   mention_counts AS mc
  JOIN   question_tags  AS qt USING (so_qid)
), UNNEST(tag_arr) AS tag
GROUP BY tag
ORDER BY total_mentions DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

These 10 queries incrementally explore the needed data, culminating in a query that delivers the requested “top 10 Stack Overflow tags most often referenced in Hacker News comments since 2014”.
